# What the owner of a view says when it hears view/closed doesn't take the place of the
# word that a typed cell was not saved (#269). tests/drive.rs installs a csv-table that
# closes its table whenever the file changes and says "heard view/closed" when it is told
# the view is closed. A year is typed when another program writes the file; Enter ends
# the typing, the view goes, and the status line says the edit was not saved, before what
# the owner said.
size 140x24
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys /
type eruptions
wait-for ▤ Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
keys enter j
wait-for CSV table · ⏎ to open it in csv-table
keys enter
wait-for Mount St. Helens  1980
keys j l e
wait-for Year: 1883▏
keys ctrl+u
type 1884
wait-for Year: 1884▏
write Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv Volcano (link),Year,VEI,Notes (markdown)\nVesuvius,79,5,\nKrakatoa,1883,6,\nTambora,1816,7,\n
wait-for its extension closed this view: what you type is not saved
keys enter
wait-for heard view/closed
wait-for not saved: csv-table had closed this view
screen
keys q
exits 0
